  "notes": "Stockholm-school pop producer/writer inside but not identical to the Max Martin camp. The Lane line names the straight class first, so `halfTime` is false and the trap-pop half-time records stay documented rather than encoded. The drum block is his: \"crisp programmed kick and clap with a very short reverb, 16th hats, and a documented fondness for a brass-or-synth stab doubling the backbeat; percussion is arranged so every section has a different hat density.\" So the snare is hard-transient under a `short` tail, `hihat.base` is 16th with the widest `fillDensity`-adjacent velocity spread here, and the stab doubling the backbeat is why `impact` sits in the perc lanes at `downbeat` placement alongside the offbeat shaker. The 808 is authored because the entry names it — \"808 sub with short glides for the trap-pop mode; pumping synth sub for the dance-pop mode\" — as `counter_riff`, with the pumping sub as the bassline. Harmony is the Swedish lift, stated plainly: \"minor-mode verses resolving to a relative-major or Lydian-bright chorus\", so `lydian` carries real weight in `scales` and a major family sits beside the minor ones; \"he plays keyboards, guitar, bass and percussion, so voicings are keyboard-idiomatic with 7ths and 9ths\" is the extension spread. The melody block is the melodic-math school itself: \"4-bar loops, hook stated twice, pre-chorus with rhythmic acceleration into the chorus\", which is `twoBarCellRepeat`, a wide `densityPerBar` for the acceleration and 2/4-bar phrases; \"brass and supersaw stabs as answer-phrases\" is the `answer_lick` counter, and \"toplines written for a specific singer's range and stacked in tight unison\" is the tight counter offset. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because the research says the parametric detail is \"partly school-conventional\": every drum probability, the humanize pair and `bpm.mode` 120 (the midpoint of the stated 100—140 working core) are INFERRED.",
